From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sergei Sveshnikov <sergei@svesh.dev>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 17:32:17 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 09/10] Import into IMAP folders under server UIDs (/svesh-api)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

When a server cannot hand out some bodies any more, a mail client's
offline copy is what is left. Upstream imports only into local accounts.

- GET  /svesh-api/archived-uids/:account_id/:mailbox_id — UIDs of the
  folder already in the archive.
- POST /svesh-api/import/:account_id/:mailbox_id?uid=&internal_date= with
  the raw message: stored like a synced one, under the given UID, so sync
  and gap-fill see it as archived; "exists" if the UID is archived.
- IMAP accounts only, admin or account:manage; outside /api/v1.
- Tests: import roundtrip and refusals; included in the fork's checks.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
